Package: martinmunk-avr-controld
Version: 0.4.0~dev1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Martin Munk Hansen <skiers.56.haggis@icloud.com>
Installed-Size: 20531
Depends: python3.13
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: Python AVR broker daemon with Home Assistant MQTT bridge
 avr-controld owns each AV receiver connection (NAD/Denon/...) and exposes it to
 Home Assistant as basic MQTT entities (power/volume/mute/input). It ships a
 self-contained virtualenv under /opt/avr-controld/venv with all Python
 dependencies bundled (nad_receiver, paho-mqtt, pyserial), so nothing is pulled
 from PyPI on the target and everything stays dpkg-tracked.
